# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/

# Application workspace state (Freebuff client) — not project content
.freebuff/

# Generated AF3 job files / export trees (regenerate with `configbuilder`)
# — root-anchored so it never matches the configbuilder/output source package
/output/

# Internal working copies (.cbproj autosave) — the application's resume state
.configbuilder/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large local reference data — kept out of the repository on purpose.
#
# `testdata/` holds two multi-megabyte MSA JSON dumps (23.4 MB and 12.0 MB).
# No test, fixture or runtime module reads them: they are reference examples of
# the protein/RNA/ligand MSA shapes, recorded in HANDOFF.md as "referenced by
# no current test". They stay on disk and out of Git so a clone stays small.
# Root-anchored: nothing under tests/fixtures/ is affected by this rule.
/testdata/

# Planning documents that describe how the project was built rather than
# what it ships. They stay on disk and untracked by decision.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
HANDOFF.md
CHECKLIST.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version-controlled project material (deliberately NOT ignored).
#
# `tests/`, `fixtures/`, `docs/` and `.github/` were excluded wholesale by the
# gate-removal commit (85a606a), which left the whole suite, its fixtures, the
# contract-pin document and the CI workflow untracked: `git ls-files tests`
# returned 0 files, so no clone could reproduce the suite's result. They are
# tracked again (gate recovery, docs/GATE_RECOVERY_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md).
#
#   tests/                   the suite, including tests/fixtures/af3_pipeline/
#   fixtures/                golden recipes, compatibility .cbproj files, builder
#   docs/                    CONTRACT_PIN.md (cited by tests), audits and reports
#   .github/                 the CI workflow that runs the suite
#   AUTHORITATIVE_SPEC.md    read by tests/contract/test_catalogue_traceability
#   DOMAIN_MAPPING.md        read by tests/contract/test_catalogue_traceability
#
# `__pycache__/` above still excludes compiled test bytecode.
#
# Deliberately kept out, even so:
#
#   af3_analysis/            the separate comparative-analysis package (out of
#                            the builder repository's scope by decision)
#   generated_jobs/          local generated output and recipes
#   .stage*                  local review screenshots and notes
#   pytest-of-*/             pytest's local temp workspace
af3_analysis/
generated_jobs/
.stage*
pytest-of-*/
# A workspace-local pytest basetemp: the GUI launch tests run the project venv
# as a child process, and on a machine whose %TEMP% that venv cannot write to
# they are run with ``--basetemp=.pytest-tmp``.
.pytest-tmp/
